course: dictionary
lesson: 16157
title: Withers: a horse's back and a fading plant
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: One word can have two different meanings, and the words around it tell you which one you need. «The pony's withers were just above my hand.» Here withers is a noun, a part of a horse's body.
explain: «The rose withers when nobody waters it.» Here withers is a verb, the form of wither. A plant withers when it dries up and dies. The sentence is about a plant, so the verb meaning fits.
explain: Ask yourself: is the word naming a thing, or is it an action? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check. «Hope withers away after a long wait» makes sense if withers means fades, so that is the meaning.
fact: The withers are the highest point of a horse's back, the ridge between its shoulder blades.
fact: Horses and ponies are measured in hands from the ground to the withers. One hand is 4 inches, about 10 cm.
fact: «Withers» is also the verb form of «wither»: a plant withers when it dries up and dies.
fact: In stories, «withers» can describe plants, hope or old age fading: «Her smile withers when she hears the news.»
fact: Phrases to remember: «height at the withers» and «withers away».
exercise: «The vet gently touched the horse's withers.» Where are a horse's withers? | Under its hooves | *On its back, between its shoulder blades | On its tail | In its mouth
exercise: «Without water, the plant withers in the hot sun.» What happens to the plant? | It starts to sing | It turns into a horse | It grows very tall | *It dries up and dies
exercise: Horses are measured in hands to the withers. How long is one hand? | About 50 cm | *About 4 inches, or about 10 cm | About 1 metre | About 1 cm
test: «Her hope withers away after a long wait.» What does withers mean here? | *Fades and dies away | Turns blue | Gets bigger and brighter | Shouts loudly
test: Which sentence uses withers as a verb? | *The rose withers when it has no water. | The withers of the hill were green. | The horse's withers were sore. | Withers is the name of a pony.
exam: A pony is 12 hands high at the withers. How tall is one hand? | *About 4 inches, or about 10 cm | About 1 foot | About 10 inches | About 1 metre
